  "source_review": {
    "definition": "Fixed degree20 real homogeneous harmonic polynomial on S2, maximize normalized L4/L2. Full231-coefficient rational dense kernel, dimension41, no magnitude cap. Corrects old Rudin-minimum naming to actual maximum direction.",
    "primary_source": "Root checked Stanton-Weinstein1981 DOI10.1017/S0305004100058229 local maximality of real highest-weight harmonic; global finite20 optimum not proved there. Sogge asymptotic order and2026Rudin bounded holomorphic bases do not prove this constant. Current finite20 closure search found none.",
    "human_method": "Re((x+i*y)^20), M2=B20/2 and M4=3B40/8, Bk=4^k*(k!)^2/(2k+1)!. Root independently recomputed these exact quantities and fourth-power ratio58188232951867590/10575651537777253. Human ratio~1.5315529249613015.",
    "independent_method": "Root clears coefficient denominators and uses symmetric integer products. It integrates first over azimuth using central binomial coefficients, then over latitude with a finite alternating binomial integral. Exact M2,M4 and their ratio match formal double-factorial moments for all five entries; independent fourth-root bounds1e-60 lie inside formal1e-18 interval.",
    "admission": "Five strict programs and full controls passed. Initial and own searches use Legendre zonal harmonics, not highest-weight reference. Damaged nonharmonic polynomial rejected; full returned result ignores claims; replay,cold export,error,nonfinite,timeout controls pass. Agent28tests pass. Checker direction omission returned and fixed before frozen admission."
  }
